1166
00:53:05,383 --> 00:53:06,784
You mean you hunted
these people down

1167
00:53:06,784 --> 00:53:09,086
and then killed them
and did that, too?

1168
00:53:09,086 --> 00:53:10,421
And finished your degree?

1169
00:53:10,421 --> 00:53:15,159
Exactly. I hunted them,
but shall I tell you why?

1170
00:53:15,159 --> 00:53:17,295
Aw, cripes, yeah, sure.

1171
00:53:17,295 --> 00:53:18,996
I've been a scholar all my life.

1172
00:53:18,996 --> 00:53:20,265
I've got a GED.

1173
00:53:20,265 --> 00:53:23,634
I was curator of a large museum
when the war began.

1174
00:53:23,634 --> 00:53:25,002
The Roger Maris Museum.

1175
00:53:25,002 --> 00:53:26,671
I who had never killed
anything in my life

1176
00:53:26,671 --> 00:53:31,175
found myself assigned to duty
as a sniper, a sharpshooter

1177
00:53:31,175 --> 00:53:33,911
because of my steady hand
and keen eyesight.

1178
00:53:33,911 --> 00:53:36,347
Fifty monologues
for male actors.

1179
00:53:36,347 --> 00:53:40,551
It amuses me now that I found it
distasteful at first.

1180
00:53:40,551 --> 00:53:42,653
Or is it distasteful
that I found out?

1181
00:53:42,653 --> 00:53:45,656
As time went by,
I adjusted my new activity.

1182
00:53:45,656 --> 00:53:46,891
Uh, sir.

1183
00:53:46,891 --> 00:53:50,227
What had been an unpleasant duty
became a pleasure.

1184
00:53:50,227 --> 00:53:53,030
Then it developed
into a passion, then
into a lust.

1185
00:53:53,030 --> 00:53:54,365
And then back into unpleasant.

1186
00:53:54,365 --> 00:53:55,966
A lust for blood.

1187
00:53:55,966 --> 00:53:58,168
A lust that has grown
with the years

1188
00:53:58,168 --> 00:54:03,173
