1213
00:55:07,705 --> 00:55:09,940
It's a little pricey,
but I think it's worth it.

1214
00:55:12,142 --> 00:55:13,811
Tony.

1215
00:55:14,879 --> 00:55:16,714
Is this your drunk, Hartley?

1216
00:55:16,714 --> 00:55:19,116
Yes. Tony.

1217
00:55:19,116 --> 00:55:20,585
Tony. Tony. Tony. Tony.

1218
00:55:20,585 --> 00:55:22,353
I think it only fair he should
be here at this time

1219
00:55:22,353 --> 00:55:25,723
because he's going to take part
in the game, too.

1220
00:55:25,723 --> 00:55:30,027
No, no, please.
Don't send me out
there with them.

1221
00:55:30,027 --> 00:55:34,365
I can't stay cool anymore.
This is gonna be so fun.

1222
00:55:34,365 --> 00:55:37,768
I've paid you well to provide me
with subjects in the past.

1223
00:55:37,768 --> 00:55:40,438
I warned you not to use
your boat for other purposes.

1224
00:55:40,438 --> 00:55:43,107
You went inner-tubing,
didn't you?

1225
00:55:43,107 --> 00:55:46,076
To allow these young people
to find their way here
without my knowledge.

1226
00:55:46,076 --> 00:55:49,046
I think it only right
you should share their fate.

1227
00:55:49,046 --> 00:55:51,949
- Do you mean...
- That's exactly what I mean.

1228
00:55:51,949 --> 00:55:55,586
Tony was my source of supply
for subjects.

1229
00:55:55,586 --> 00:55:59,256
In the past, they were
always convicts escaped
from the penal island.

1230
00:55:59,256 --> 00:56:00,925
- ( laughing )
- Stop it.

1231
00:56:00,925 --> 00:56:02,627
Now I find him no
longer dependable.

1232
00:56:02,627 --> 00:56:05,396
Do you really think
you can get away
with this madness?

1233
00:56:05,396 --> 00:56:09,534
Madness? But I've planned us
a pleasant evening's diversion.

1234
00:56:09,534 --> 00:56:12,603
See, I knew he was only kidding.
That's just a toy.

1235
00:56:12,603 --> 00:56:14,238
That couldn't kill anyone.

1236
00:56:14,238 --> 00:56:16,441
You're forgetting
about the boiled heads,
aren't you?

1237
00:56:16,441 --> 00:56:19,009
- Is that Alf on the wall?
- I hope so.

1238
00:56:21,145 --> 00:56:23,514
Somebody took my bones.

1239
00:56:25,382 --> 00:56:29,754
It amuses me and is
also distasteful that
you think that I would--

1240
00:56:32,490 --> 00:56:35,292
Did I hit him?

1241
00:56:37,795 --> 00:56:40,030
Well, that threw
cold water on everything.

1242
00:56:40,030 --> 00:56:42,900
I guess it could
kill somebody.

1243
00:56:42,900 --> 00:56:44,869
Yes, it can.

1244
00:56:44,869 --> 00:56:46,370
Now go change your pants.

1245
00:56:46,370 --> 00:56:48,272
Soon we'll try to prove it.

1246
00:56:48,272 --> 00:56:51,876
- Please, Mr. Balleau,
don't do this awful thing.
- Oh, please.

1247
00:56:51,876 --> 00:56:53,911
You have nothing to be alarmed
about, young lady.

1248
00:56:53,911 --> 00:56:58,849
You're in no danger.
Either of you. Your life here
with me will be a pleasant one.

1249
00:56:58,849 --> 00:57:01,652
You'll find me a most
accommodating host.

1250
00:57:01,652 --> 00:57:04,655
You think Jeanne and I
will have anything to do
with you

1251
00:57:04,655 --> 00:57:07,257
if you send Pete and Johnny out
and kill them in that jungle?

1252
00:57:07,257 --> 00:57:09,894
Yes, I think so. 
 I know so.

1253
00:57:09,894 --> 00:57:12,863
No one has ever left this island
dead or alive.

1254
00:57:12,863 --> 00:57:17,735
Since the unfortunate incident
involving my wife has left me
without feminine company...

1255
00:57:17,735 --> 00:57:20,137
Except for Minnie Pearl.

1256
00:57:20,137 --> 00:57:23,273
...to getting to now
you both better, much better.

1257
00:57:23,273 --> 00:57:25,843
He bounces back from
a bad relationship.

1258
00:57:25,843 --> 00:57:27,211
...sitting ducks out
of Pete and me.

1259
00:57:27,211 --> 00:57:29,046
Do you have to hurt
the girls, too?

1260
00:57:29,046 --> 00:57:30,447
Hurt them?

1261
00:57:30,447 --> 00:57:33,851
Johnny, he really means it.
What are we gonna do?

1262
00:57:33,851 --> 00:57:37,087
Oh, how'd that get there?

1263
00:57:37,087 --> 00:57:39,924
...wrong person about
your future activity.

1264
00:57:39,924 --> 00:57:42,026
Go with Jondor.

1265
00:57:42,026 --> 00:57:45,229
Jondor, lock them in their room
and then come back at once.

1266
00:57:45,229 --> 00:57:49,867
His real name's Clint,
but Jondor has a certain ring.

1267
00:57:49,867 --> 00:57:52,469
It does.

1268
00:57:52,469 --> 00:57:55,105
Well, he's
kind of cute, I guess.

1269
00:57:55,105 --> 00:57:56,541
I can change him.

1270
00:58:01,712 --> 00:58:04,348
All right, madman.

1271
00:58:04,348 --> 00:58:06,817
But to return
to your question, Pete.

1272
00:58:06,817 --> 00:58:09,554
I know just exactly what to
do up to a certain point.

1273
00:58:09,554 --> 00:58:11,789
The rest will be up to you.

1274
00:58:11,789 --> 00:58:15,492
Are you listening to this, Tony?
It applies to you, too.

1275
00:58:15,492 --> 00:58:19,730
Moonlight's bright tonight
so you will make your way to
the starting point of the chase.

1276
00:58:19,730 --> 00:58:21,532
It's in the center
of the jungle.

1277
00:58:21,532 --> 00:58:23,233
Eyeball will give you
exact directions.

1278
00:58:23,233 --> 00:58:24,334
Eyeball?

1279
00:58:24,334 --> 00:58:27,004
The natives used to call
it the Tree of Death.

1280
00:58:27,004 --> 00:58:28,272
I call it Bernie.

1281
00:58:28,272 --> 00:58:29,907
I'll give you plenty of time
to plan your flight

1282
00:58:29,907 --> 00:58:31,742
before I follow
with the crossbow

1283
00:58:31,742 --> 00:58:35,079
and just three of these.

1284
00:58:35,079 --> 00:58:37,748
Just three shots.
That's all I allow myself.

1285
00:58:37,748 --> 00:58:38,983
Or else I get silly.

1286
00:58:38,983 --> 00:58:41,251
Very sporting,
don't you think?

1287
00:58:41,251 --> 00:58:44,722
- Ah, Eyeball.
- It's Jondor, sir.

1288
00:58:44,722 --> 00:58:47,958
Don't you think it's very
sporting of me to allow
myself just one chance

1289
00:58:47,958 --> 00:58:49,259
at each of you?

1290
00:58:49,259 --> 00:58:52,229
Oh, sure, real sporting.

1291
00:58:52,229 --> 00:58:54,599
Frankly, I'm steamed.

1292
00:58:54,599 --> 00:58:57,401
In a jungle that you know
like the palm of your hand?

1293
00:58:57,401 --> 00:59:00,738
With that thing that could
knock an elephant over?
You're gonna hunt us down.

1294
00:59:00,738 --> 00:59:02,807
We have nothing 
 to defend ourselves with.

1295
00:59:02,807 --> 00:59:05,142
Not so fast.
Not so fast.

1296
00:59:05,142 --> 00:59:08,779
You haven't allowed me to finish
the entire plan of the evening's
entertainment.

1297
00:59:08,779 --> 00:59:10,314
There will be
a light deck lunch.

1298
00:59:10,314 --> 00:59:12,750
Here, catch.

1299
00:59:12,750 --> 00:59:14,619
Where do you drink out
of this thing?

1300
00:59:14,619 --> 00:59:17,755
Tony, it isn't loaded.

1301
00:59:17,755 --> 00:59:21,291
Neither am I.
Oh, please just a taste.

1302
00:59:21,291 --> 00:59:24,194
...unloaded gun.

1303
00:59:24,194 --> 00:59:27,732
It's time to start.
The odds are not
completely one-sided.

1304
00:59:27,732 --> 00:59:31,535
Your youth and numbers
against my skill
and experience.

1305
00:59:31,535 --> 00:59:35,139
You'll find the ammunition
in the branches of the Tree
of Death.

1306
00:59:35,139 --> 00:59:37,608
When that gun is loaded,

1307
00:59:37,608 --> 00:59:40,845
my life will also be subject
to how the hunt goes.

1308
00:59:40,845 --> 00:59:42,980
Tonight on
"The Hollywood Palace."

1309
00:59:45,382 --> 00:59:47,384
Oh. Oh, real good plan.

1310
00:59:47,384 --> 00:59:50,154
Let's go to the Tree
of Death right away.

1311
00:59:53,357 --> 00:59:56,260
Maybe there's a map that tells
the way to the Tree of Death.

1312
00:59:56,260 --> 00:59:58,495
Mr. Owl! Who-who!

1313
00:59:58,495 --> 01:00:00,965
Tree of Novelty Items.

1314
01:00:00,965 --> 01:00:02,667
Here it is. I found it.

1315
01:00:02,667 --> 01:00:04,068
It's Meow Meow Kitty.

1316
01:00:04,068 --> 01:00:06,003
( meows )

1317
01:00:07,504 --> 01:00:09,907
Why, that rat.

1318
01:00:09,907 --> 01:00:12,810
That lousy stinking rat.

1319
01:00:12,810 --> 01:00:15,479
Let's not call his names.
It'll escalate into bitterness.

1320
01:00:15,479 --> 01:00:17,047
He left only one shell.

1321
01:00:17,047 --> 01:00:19,383
That's the way his
twisted mind works.

1322
01:00:19,383 --> 01:00:20,384
I don't like a villain.

1323
01:00:20,384 --> 01:00:22,019
What do you mean?

1324
01:00:22,019 --> 01:00:24,855
He allows himself three shots,
one for each of us.

1325
01:00:24,855 --> 01:00:26,891
But we get one shot at him.

1326
01:00:26,891 --> 01:00:29,559
I'm just about fed up.

1327
01:00:29,559 --> 01:00:31,461
Come on, give me the gun
and let's get moving.

1328
01:00:31,461 --> 01:00:34,364
No, you don't, buster.
You just hand over that bullet.

1329
01:00:34,364 --> 01:00:38,568
- Don't be a fool, Tony. I'm a
better shot than you are.
- Yeah?

1330
01:00:38,568 --> 01:00:41,005
What are you saying,
I'm a drunk?

1331
01:00:41,005 --> 01:00:43,640
I slapped Ann B. Davis once.

1332
01:00:43,640 --> 01:00:46,276
- No.
- I have.

1333
01:00:46,276 --> 01:00:49,513
And I ain't taking any chances
on no amateur.

1334
01:00:50,948 --> 01:00:54,651
( imitates gunshot )
Whoops.

1335
01:00:54,651 --> 01:00:56,153
Are you done?

1336
01:00:56,153 --> 01:00:58,355
Which way should we go?

1337
01:00:58,355 --> 01:01:02,827
I don't know which way
you two guys are going,
but I'm going alone.

1338
01:01:02,827 --> 01:01:05,362
- So long, suckers.
- Hey!

1339
01:01:05,362 --> 01:01:07,097
Now that was really rude.

1340
01:01:07,097 --> 01:01:09,399
Wait, come back here!

1341
01:01:09,399 --> 01:01:11,368
I liked him.

1342
01:01:11,368 --> 01:01:13,337
It's better if we do split up.
It doubles our chances.

1343
01:01:13,337 --> 01:01:15,840
- How?
- Balleau can't hunt
in two directions at once.

1344
01:01:15,840 --> 01:01:17,607
Now look.
The way I figure

1345
01:01:17,607 --> 01:01:19,543
it we must be right about
in the middle of the island.

1346
01:01:19,543 --> 01:01:21,979
We'll head that way,
try to get to the beach.

1347
01:01:21,979 --> 01:01:24,281
Then work our way back
to the house.

1348
01:01:24,281 --> 01:01:25,449
Back to the house?
Are you nuts?

1349
01:01:25,449 --> 01:01:27,584
I've got a slight dementia.

1350
01:01:27,584 --> 01:01:30,287
- Let's try to find the boat.
- We've gotta try and get
the girls out first.

1351
01:01:30,287 --> 01:01:31,989
Balleau said he wouldn't touch--

1352
01:01:31,989 --> 01:01:33,190
Never mind what he said.
I know what he meant.

1353
01:01:33,190 --> 01:01:35,392
Filthy unchristian sex.

1354
01:01:35,392 --> 01:01:37,661
He just kept looking
at the girls. Come on,
let's get started.

1355
01:01:37,661 --> 01:01:39,596
I just don't see
how you figure--

1356
01:01:39,596 --> 01:01:42,232
Never mind.
We gotta do what we can.

1357
01:01:42,232 --> 01:01:43,600
That's the first thing.

1358
01:01:43,600 --> 01:01:46,203
They found the Tree
of Interminable Dialogue.

1359
01:01:47,972 --> 01:01:51,508
Here's hoping we find the second
thing, whatever that will be.

1360
01:01:51,508 --> 01:01:53,477
Heard that.

1361
01:01:53,477 --> 01:01:56,413
I'm almost ready, mad doctor
dear. Just freshening up.

1362
01:01:56,413 --> 01:01:59,216
The guard is still out there
and wide awake.

1363
01:01:59,216 --> 01:02:01,185
And cute.

1364
01:02:01,185 --> 01:02:04,488
Even if we do get out
of this room, where
are we gonna go?

1365
01:02:04,488 --> 01:02:05,589
I don't know.

1366
01:02:05,589 --> 01:02:06,891
We can have a slumber party.

1367
01:02:06,891 --> 01:02:09,894
Maybe we could find the boys
and try to get to the boat.

1368
01:02:09,894 --> 01:02:12,963
We don't even know
where it is.

1369
01:02:12,963 --> 01:02:14,865
It's just no use.

1370
01:02:14,865 --> 01:02:19,503
* Where is love *

1371
01:02:19,503 --> 01:02:22,639
Am I thinking what
I'm thinking? Hmm?

1372
01:02:24,909 --> 01:02:26,343
Use your weighty hulk.

1373
01:02:26,343 --> 01:02:29,013
Even this window is locked.

1374
01:02:31,681 --> 01:02:33,951
Even the spittoon is locked.

1375
01:02:33,951 --> 01:02:36,253
I could make placements
for the children.

1376
01:02:38,355 --> 01:02:39,623
Come here, Jeanne.

1377
01:02:39,623 --> 01:02:42,292
Move it, move it, move it!

1378
01:02:42,292 --> 01:02:45,996
Listen to me.
I've got an idea.

1379
01:02:45,996 --> 01:02:49,433
Don't ask any questions.
Just do exactly as I say.

1380
01:02:49,433 --> 01:02:51,701
What do you want me to do?

1381
01:02:51,701 --> 01:02:52,837
- Here.
- Oh.

1382
01:02:52,837 --> 01:02:56,406
I'm Blind Tom, yarrgh!

1383
01:02:56,406 --> 01:02:57,441
( clattering )

1384
01:02:57,441 --> 01:02:58,976
Just set that anywhere.

1385
01:03:02,479 --> 01:03:05,015
Oh, I'm terribly sorry.

1386
01:03:05,015 --> 01:03:06,383
Not the Ming spittoon.

1387
01:03:06,383 --> 01:03:09,987
I was moving it
and it just broke.

1388
01:03:09,987 --> 01:03:13,423
I'm sure I can fix it.
Can you get me some glue?

1389
01:03:13,423 --> 01:03:15,125
This is their cutest plan yet.

1390
01:03:15,125 --> 01:03:16,360
I didn't mean to break it.

1391
01:03:16,360 --> 01:03:17,661
Broke.

1392
01:03:17,661 --> 01:03:19,496
It was such a pretty vase.

1393
01:03:19,496 --> 01:03:22,967
Damn you all to hell.

1394
01:03:22,967 --> 01:03:24,668
( laughing )

1395
01:03:24,668 --> 01:03:27,771
New stuff killed.

1396
01:03:28,873 --> 01:03:30,507
Jeanne, come on, hurry.

1397
01:03:30,507 --> 01:03:32,342
But we need to fix the vase.

1398
01:03:32,342 --> 01:03:33,710
Come on, I'll help you
climb out.

1399
01:03:33,710 --> 01:03:36,180
Out there?
But we'll be killed.

1400
01:03:36,180 --> 01:03:38,482
No, we won't.
There's a ledge out there.

1401
01:03:38,482 --> 01:03:40,717
We can work along that
till we come to an open window.

1402
01:03:40,717 --> 01:03:42,686
- But what if--
- Never mind. It's the only way.

1403
01:03:42,686 --> 01:03:44,488
Come on. Hurry up.

1404
01:03:44,488 --> 01:03:45,789
Be careful, too.

1405
01:03:45,789 --> 01:03:47,624
Now fly, monkeys, fly!

1406
01:03:47,624 --> 01:03:49,793
( hums )

1407
01:03:57,501 --> 01:03:59,169
Action foliage.

1408
01:04:01,371 --> 01:04:03,941
Jondor, heel.

1409
01:04:03,941 --> 01:04:06,343
I got a head boiling.
I should be getting back.

1410
01:04:06,343 --> 01:04:10,347
Chopping your own Christmas tree
is harder than you think.

1411
01:04:13,283 --> 01:04:16,186
When did he get nude?

1412
01:04:16,186 --> 01:04:18,322
God, I admire his jacket.

1413
01:04:20,824 --> 01:04:22,559
Brian Benben.

1414
01:04:24,661 --> 01:04:27,497
Man, is he Flemish.

1415
01:04:27,497 --> 01:04:29,633
I love you this much.

1416
01:04:29,633 --> 01:04:32,636
Don't tell me.
We've come to the end
of the trail.

1417
01:04:32,636 --> 01:04:35,505
The soul trail.

1418
01:04:35,505 --> 01:04:37,975
No, no, it's broken, honey.

1419
01:04:37,975 --> 01:04:40,144
I'm disappointed in you, Tony.

1420
01:04:40,144 --> 01:04:44,114
You've known me long enough
to realize I wouldn't give you
a gun without first taking

1421
01:04:44,114 --> 01:04:46,483
the precaution of removing
the firing pin.

1422
01:04:46,483 --> 01:04:48,418
And the distributor cap.

1423
01:04:50,054 --> 01:04:52,656
Do you find that hard
to believe?

1424
01:04:52,656 --> 01:04:55,825
You see, Tony,
if I hadn't given you the gun,

1425
01:04:55,825 --> 01:04:57,995
you would never have given me
the pleasure

1426
01:04:57,995 --> 01:05:00,397
of seeing your face
at the moment of the kill.

1427
01:05:00,397 --> 01:05:03,900
Wait, it's not a pleasure.

1428
01:05:03,900 --> 01:05:07,637
Please, don't do it, please,
I'll never give your
secret away.

1429
01:05:07,637 --> 01:05:11,341
I promise. I'll get
you more convicts.

1430
01:05:11,341 --> 01:05:12,742
I'll be your best friend.

1431
01:05:12,742 --> 01:05:15,312
I'll never make
a mistake again, please.

1432
01:05:15,312 --> 01:05:17,581
I got candy bars in my room.

1433
01:05:17,581 --> 01:05:20,817
All right, Tony,
I'll reconsider.

1434
01:05:20,817 --> 01:05:22,719
But I already have
a best friend, bye.

1435
01:05:22,719 --> 01:05:24,955
Thank you.

1436
01:05:24,955 --> 01:05:26,923
Can I borrow a shirt
by the way?

1437
01:05:26,923 --> 01:05:29,026
You won't be sorry.

1438
01:05:29,026 --> 01:05:30,794
Enough of this.
I have work to do.

1439
01:05:30,794 --> 01:05:35,099
- You get back to the house.
- Yes, sir, I'll go right now.

1440
01:05:35,099 --> 01:05:38,202
I'll make you so proud of me.

1441
01:05:38,202 --> 01:05:39,970
Tony.

1442
01:05:39,970 --> 01:05:43,207
I lied.

1443
01:05:43,207 --> 01:05:45,709
I have reconsidered.

1444
01:05:45,709 --> 01:05:49,413
John Steinbeck in
"Of Mice and Murder."

1445
01:05:49,413 --> 01:05:50,614
( screaming )

1446
01:05:50,614 --> 01:05:54,618
Rail, rail against
the dying of the-- ugh!

1447
01:05:56,486 --> 01:05:58,822
Well, that was a good one.

1448
01:05:58,822 --> 01:06:01,025
I'm sure I heard a scream.

1449
01:06:01,025 --> 01:06:03,960
That figures.
Boy, am I cheesed.

1450
01:06:03,960 --> 01:06:05,962
I think it might just have
been a jungle bird.

1451
01:06:05,962 --> 01:06:09,533
No, I'm sure it was--
I'm sure it was Tony.
That means we're next.

1452
01:06:09,533 --> 01:06:11,568
Come on, Johnny, let's try
and find that boat.

1453
01:06:11,568 --> 01:06:13,237
It's our only chance.

1454
01:06:13,237 --> 01:06:17,007
We're not gonna do anything
until we get the girls free.
Come on.

1455
01:06:17,007 --> 01:06:19,076
The war's this way.

1456
01:06:24,948 --> 01:06:28,585
What are doing?
No, I don't want your filth.

1457
01:06:28,585 --> 01:06:31,888
Hurry, back to the
Tree of Death. We'll pick up
the other trail there.

1458
01:06:31,888 --> 01:06:35,859
It would be ironic
if the Tree of Death
got Dutch Elm Disease.

1459
01:06:35,859 --> 01:06:37,894
Yeah, "Stump of Death"
wouldn't be the same.

1460
01:06:37,894 --> 01:06:39,729
No.

1461
01:06:39,729 --> 01:06:44,268
Aha, we're back
to our room, see? Oh.

1462
01:06:44,268 --> 01:06:46,370
Oh, it's like "Cagney and Lacey,
the Attractive Years."

1463
01:06:46,370 --> 01:06:48,805
"Snoop Sisters,
the Early Days."

1464
01:06:48,805 --> 01:06:51,875
"Where Angles Go,
Trouble Follows."

1465
01:06:51,875 --> 01:06:54,178
Well, we made it this far.

1466
01:06:54,178 --> 01:06:56,280
Yeah, but where
is "this far"?

1467
01:06:56,280 --> 01:06:59,116
I don't know, but it's
closer to far away than
back in that room.

1468
01:06:59,116 --> 01:07:00,850
You're deep.

1469
01:07:00,850 --> 01:07:03,920
Let's do the whole thing
over again. It was fun.

1470
01:07:06,223 --> 01:07:10,060
I just wanna see the boiled
heads. It'd be too bad to come
all the way to this island

1471
01:07:10,060 --> 01:07:11,928
and not see the boiled heads.

1472
01:07:13,897 --> 01:07:17,033
Betty, my pants have
reached a crisis point.

1473
01:07:17,033 --> 01:07:21,471
Come on, we have to find
the secret to bock beer.

1474
01:07:21,471 --> 01:07:26,476
Oh, no, that's the door
to that terrible workroom
I told you about.

1475
01:07:26,476 --> 01:07:30,046
Oh. Wait a minute.

1476
01:07:30,046 --> 01:07:32,416
Maybe we can find a knife
or something in there.

1477
01:07:32,416 --> 01:07:34,618
Then we can bone some ham.

1478
01:07:34,618 --> 01:07:36,320
Come on.

1479
01:07:37,621 --> 01:07:40,724
- I'll go first.
- You've met the heads.

1480
01:07:42,526 --> 01:07:46,363
You know, they could
wear the heads and then
escape as someone else.

1481
01:07:46,363 --> 01:07:50,066
You've gotta believe me.
There were heads all
over the place.

1482
01:07:50,066 --> 01:07:52,302
Hey. The boulya's is done.

1483
01:07:52,302 --> 01:07:55,339
We gotta get a couple of these
that we can carry easily.

1484
01:07:55,339 --> 01:07:58,708
It's no use,
Betty. Even if we did, I
couldn't use one anyway.

1485
01:07:58,708 --> 01:08:00,544
Jeanne, listen to me.

1486
01:08:00,544 --> 01:08:04,781
Nobody expects
the Spanish Inquisition.

1487
01:08:04,781 --> 01:08:07,217
I'm Pegleg Dick.

1488
01:08:07,217 --> 01:08:08,618
Keep away from us.

1489
01:08:08,618 --> 01:08:11,621
So you want hush puppies
or rice pilaf with
your lobster?

1490
01:08:11,621 --> 01:08:14,791
...I'll use this.
Jeanne, run to the door.
He can only get one of us.

1491
01:08:14,791 --> 01:08:17,727
Mr. Balleau told me to take
good care of you, ladies.

1492
01:08:17,727 --> 01:08:20,897
Don't come any closer.

1493
01:08:20,897 --> 01:08:22,432
Can't you see I'm harmless?

1494
01:08:22,432 --> 01:08:23,667
Isn't everyone here phony?

1495
01:08:23,667 --> 01:08:26,503
I'm not trying to hurt you.

1496
01:08:26,503 --> 01:08:28,205
( screaming )

1497
01:08:28,205 --> 01:08:30,106
This doesn't involve you,
Betty.

1498
01:08:31,508 --> 01:08:33,710
( laughs )

1499
01:08:33,710 --> 01:08:34,944
( laughs )

1500
01:08:34,944 --> 01:08:39,183
Can't you see?
Can't you see?

1501
01:08:39,183 --> 01:08:42,085
Bob Packwood goes a-courtin'.

1502
01:08:42,085 --> 01:08:45,922
So do you maybe wanna go out
and have coffee sometime?

1503
01:08:45,922 --> 01:08:48,592
Ugh!

1504
01:08:48,592 --> 01:08:50,927
( screaming )

1505
01:08:52,896 --> 01:08:55,499
( screaming )

1506
01:08:55,499 --> 01:08:57,601
Okay, half off the soup today.

1507
01:08:59,703 --> 01:09:01,971
( shouts )

1508
01:09:01,971 --> 01:09:04,140
Jeez, he looks younger already.

1509
01:09:05,375 --> 01:09:07,177
( gulping )

1510
01:09:07,177 --> 01:09:10,180
Wait, I still haven't
seen the heads.

1511
01:09:10,180 --> 01:09:11,915
That was fun.
Who's next?

1512
01:09:13,049 --> 01:09:14,984
( shouts )

1513
01:09:14,984 --> 01:09:18,488
I think I heard the girls say
that if we were ever captured
by an evil hunter,

1514
01:09:18,488 --> 01:09:21,090
to go ahead without 'em, okay?

1515
01:09:21,090 --> 01:09:24,428
We're lost.
What's the use?

1516
01:09:24,428 --> 01:09:28,097
It's only a matter of time
before Balleau catches up
with us.

1517
01:09:28,097 --> 01:09:30,867
I don't think we are lost.
The jungle is thinning out.

1518
01:09:30,867 --> 01:09:32,101
We must be getting closer
to the beach.

1519
01:09:32,101 --> 01:09:34,103
I think that still
qualifies as lost.

1520
01:09:34,103 --> 01:09:37,707
So what? I don't mean
to put you down, Johnny.

1521
01:09:37,707 --> 01:09:39,343
But you suck.

1522
01:09:39,343 --> 01:09:43,380
- If we do find the beach,
then what are we--
- Hold it.

1523
01:09:43,380 --> 01:09:47,116
Hey Jondor, has my latest
Ted Nugent bow hunting
magazine come yet?

1524
01:09:48,752 --> 01:09:51,221
Come on, we gotta make time.

1525
01:09:51,221 --> 01:09:53,357
Be gentle. Oh.

1526
01:09:53,357 --> 01:09:57,026
He's in a scene with Robert Reed
and he's the weenie.

1527
01:09:57,026 --> 01:10:00,163
( screaming )

1528
01:10:01,531 --> 01:10:03,333
Someone's got allergies.

1529
01:10:03,333 --> 01:10:04,634
Don't make a sound.

1530
01:10:06,770 --> 01:10:11,140
- ( laughing )
- Look, John the Baptist.

1531
01:10:11,140 --> 01:10:13,810
They haven't seen us yet.

1532
01:10:13,810 --> 01:10:15,144
Back off.

1533
01:10:15,144 --> 01:10:17,581
I think it's Charlie Callas.

1534
01:10:17,581 --> 01:10:20,350
Can I just get some service?

1535
01:10:25,855 --> 01:10:27,724
I can't get out.

1536
01:10:27,724 --> 01:10:30,260
Hi, can I help you?
I mean-- ( screaming )

1537
01:10:31,728 --> 01:10:33,497
It's quicksand.

1538
01:10:33,497 --> 01:10:36,466
Struggle. Keep quiet.

1539
01:10:38,835 --> 01:10:42,439
Come on, play Old Testament
prophet with me.

1540
01:10:44,874 --> 01:10:47,143
Later. Later.

1541
01:10:50,714 --> 01:10:53,317
No, my muffins.

1542
01:10:53,317 --> 01:10:58,021
Something scared him.
We gotta get out of here, too.

1543
01:10:58,021 --> 01:11:00,757
Next year let's just go
to Branson, Missouri.

1544
01:11:00,757 --> 01:11:04,027
I can't. I can't make it,
Johnny.

1545
01:11:04,027 --> 01:11:06,630
I just can't make it.

1546
01:11:06,630 --> 01:11:09,198
Okay, see ya.

1547
01:11:09,198 --> 01:11:12,769
Here, I want you
to have this shirt.

1548
01:11:12,769 --> 01:11:16,272
Hey, I'm missing one
of my leeches.

1549
01:11:16,272 --> 01:11:17,607
Get 'em off!

1550
01:11:17,607 --> 01:11:20,544
You take some off, too.
I'll meet you halfway.

1551
01:11:25,214 --> 01:11:28,184
* The night they
invented champagne *

1552
01:11:30,587 --> 01:11:33,857
- I think we found a weak link
in the security system.
- ( laughing )

1553
01:11:37,193 --> 01:11:39,329
That's the one.
He's the cute one.

1554
01:11:56,112 --> 01:11:58,415
Hello, welcome to tonight's

1555
01:11:58,415 --> 01:12:01,751
mystery murder dinner party.

1556
01:12:01,751 --> 01:12:03,520
- I did it.
- Crow!

1557
01:12:03,520 --> 01:12:06,723
- Jeez, ruined everything.
- For crying out loud!

1558
01:12:08,224 --> 01:12:10,760
I can't believe that.

1559
01:12:10,760 --> 01:12:14,364
( sniffs )
Ooh. Hey, is this whole pie for
me?

1560
01:12:16,199 --> 01:12:17,200
Whoops.

1561
01:12:17,200 --> 01:12:19,969
( music playing )

1562
01:12:22,572 --> 01:12:25,709
Yeah, turns out Rosebud
was his sled.

1563
01:12:25,709 --> 01:12:27,844
Yeah, and then "Crying Game"--

1564
01:12:27,844 --> 01:12:29,345
Hey, hey, that's--

1565
01:12:29,345 --> 01:12:31,615
You think you can make it?

1566
01:12:31,615 --> 01:12:33,883
I got a choice?

1567
01:12:33,883 --> 01:12:37,554
Boy, I feel really good.
I think I needed that
blood-letting.

1568
01:12:37,554 --> 01:12:40,790
- Sure you don't wanna check
my butt for leeches?
- Yes, I'm sure.

1569
01:12:42,492 --> 01:12:44,728
I may get a rash
from my wet pants.

1570
01:12:45,895 --> 01:12:47,797
Ahh, take that.

1571
01:12:47,797 --> 01:12:50,199
Chivalry in case
a woman comes by.

1572
01:12:52,268 --> 01:12:55,338
"The Defiant Debs."

1573
01:12:55,338 --> 01:12:56,973
Ow!

1574
01:12:56,973 --> 01:13:00,376
- Are you hurt?
- No, just my dignity.

1575
01:13:00,376 --> 01:13:02,746
And my ankle's shattered.

1576
01:13:02,746 --> 01:13:05,014
We're out of that awful house.

1577
01:13:05,014 --> 01:13:07,016
Now we'll have to try
and find the boys.

1578
01:13:07,016 --> 01:13:09,152
I just hope Balleau doesn't
find them first.

1579
01:13:09,152 --> 01:13:11,187
This is "The Osterman Weekend."

1580
01:13:13,557 --> 01:13:17,761
Oh, look at this.
The castle's this way.
Come with me.

1581
01:13:17,761 --> 01:13:19,863
Daddy keeps his porno.

1582
01:13:19,863 --> 01:13:22,331
Twice tonight you've given our
position away and now you can't
even find the trail.

1583
01:13:22,331 --> 01:13:25,368
Well, boss, you see, I got
this pinched sciatic nerve.

1584
01:13:30,406 --> 01:13:34,210
Oh, cold, oh, cold.

1585
01:13:34,210 --> 01:13:37,380
...your own stupidity
will save me the trouble
of getting rid of you.

1586
01:13:37,380 --> 01:13:40,950
If I could just voice
an objection. ( gagging )

1587
01:13:40,950 --> 01:13:44,053
The leeches will do
their work so well.

1588
01:13:44,053 --> 01:13:48,792
You might have made an
interesting specimen for my
museum.

1589
01:13:48,792 --> 01:13:49,926
( screaming )

1590
01:13:49,926 --> 01:13:51,961
Oh, that's my ride.

1591
01:13:51,961 --> 01:13:53,463
I'm sorry, Jondor.

1592
01:13:53,463 --> 01:13:54,798
Oh, you are not.

1593
01:13:54,798 --> 01:13:56,866
I won't be able to stay
to enjoy your last moments,

1594
01:13:56,866 --> 01:14:00,169
for I am urgently required
elsewhere.

1595
01:14:00,169 --> 01:14:03,039
Where are the blank checks
by the way? Well, I'll
find them.

1596
01:14:03,039 --> 01:14:05,609
Visit the La Brea Tar Pits.

1597
01:14:07,376 --> 01:14:09,378
Okay?

1598
01:14:09,378 --> 01:14:10,379
It's all right.

1599
01:14:10,379 --> 01:14:11,548
We better keep moving then.

1600
01:14:11,548 --> 01:14:13,282
We'll never find the boys
just sitting here.

1601
01:14:13,282 --> 01:14:15,852
- May I say it just
once more please?
- What?

1602
01:14:15,852 --> 01:14:16,986
Member.

1603
01:14:16,986 --> 01:14:18,187
I'm scared.

1604
01:14:18,187 --> 01:14:20,990
If it makes you feel
any better, so am I.

1605
01:14:20,990 --> 01:14:23,993
But we've got to go on.

1606
01:14:23,993 --> 01:14:27,697
Just tuck the bone back
under the skin.

1607
01:14:27,697 --> 01:14:29,098
Let's go.

1608
01:14:29,098 --> 01:14:31,801
Seems like you need a pants horn
to get into those things.

1609
01:14:34,904 --> 01:14:37,073
- ( yells )
- ( screaming )

1610
01:14:39,809 --> 01:14:40,810
Chew!

1611
01:14:40,810 --> 01:14:43,312
- That's Betty.
- And Jeanne.

1612
01:14:43,312 --> 01:14:45,048
And weird guy!

1613
01:14:46,415 --> 01:14:49,252
Let me baptize
you just once.

1614
01:14:52,321 --> 01:14:54,791
How about next Wednesday then?

1615
01:14:56,560 --> 01:14:59,596
This guy always sits next
to me on the bus.

1616
01:15:00,964 --> 01:15:03,667
It amuses me that someone
is chewing the scenery.

1617
01:15:11,207 --> 01:15:12,842
Your island is really
very not-- oh!

1618
01:15:12,842 --> 01:15:14,878
He culls the weak
from the herd.

1619
01:15:16,780 --> 01:15:20,049
Robert Reed is Buford T. Pusser
in "Prancing Tall."

1620
01:15:21,484 --> 01:15:22,552
You all right?

1621
01:15:22,552 --> 01:15:24,888
Have we had the clambake yet?

1622
01:15:24,888 --> 01:15:26,890
Let's get out of here fast.

1623
01:15:26,890 --> 01:15:30,126
I wish they'd invent computers
so I'd have somewhere to belong.

1624
01:15:31,728 --> 01:15:34,330
- This movie's back on track.
- Hmm.

1625
01:15:37,801 --> 01:15:40,670
Huh? Ew.

1626
01:15:41,971 --> 01:15:44,574
- Eww.
- Back at it.

1627
01:15:44,574 --> 01:15:47,510
I think it's the others
who are crazy.

1628
01:15:47,510 --> 01:15:50,546
I blew it. I should
have said, "Ew-eh",

1629
01:15:50,546 --> 01:15:53,249
instead of, "Eh".

1630
01:15:53,249 --> 01:15:55,451
You're looking well.

1631
01:15:55,451 --> 01:16:00,223
I had thought to permit you
to enjoy the hospitality
of my islands.

1632
01:16:00,223 --> 01:16:02,225
while I took care
of more pressing business.

1633
01:16:02,225 --> 01:16:05,261
Can I get a grunt
in here edgewise?

1634
01:16:05,261 --> 01:16:08,998
I'd rather die than have to
listen to that guy talk.

1635
01:16:08,998 --> 01:16:11,300
( screaming in pain )

1636
01:16:11,300 --> 01:16:13,236
It kind of hurts.

1637
01:16:20,376 --> 01:16:22,712
Oh, so it's you.

1638
01:16:27,050 --> 01:16:30,486
Reduce, recycle, reuse.

1639
01:16:30,486 --> 01:16:32,989
Older men always
carry handkerchiefs.

1640
01:16:32,989 --> 01:16:34,557
And this is why.

1641
01:16:36,225 --> 01:16:38,662
I'm kind of anal
about this stuff.

1642
01:16:41,097 --> 01:16:44,901
Okay, call me if there's
any pain or discomfort.

1643
01:16:44,901 --> 01:16:48,705
Been good talking
to you. So long.

1644
01:16:48,705 --> 01:16:50,840
You know,
he may be in danger

1645
01:16:50,840 --> 01:16:53,242
of over-harvesting
the game.

1646
01:16:55,044 --> 01:16:57,613
I think they're letting
us in on details we really
don't need to know.

1647
01:16:57,613 --> 01:16:58,581
Yeah.

1648
01:17:00,750 --> 01:17:02,952
The Kraut is a lonely hunter.

1649
01:17:06,355 --> 01:17:10,026
I should just put in some
strip malls and be done
with it.

1650
01:17:11,227 --> 01:17:14,030
Really not a lot to do
on this island.

1651
01:17:21,004 --> 01:17:23,873
Looks like a really
uncomfortable crotch.

1652
01:17:23,873 --> 01:17:26,575
I don't know how long we can
hold on to this kind of luck.

1653
01:17:26,575 --> 01:17:29,512
If Balleau doesn't get us,
the stream will.

1654
01:17:29,512 --> 01:17:31,681
We're gonna have to try
a real grandstand play.

1655
01:17:31,681 --> 01:17:35,251
( imitating marching band )

1656
01:17:35,251 --> 01:17:38,154
I'd say the whole bunch
is out looking for us.

1657
01:17:38,154 --> 01:17:41,490
Good. At least they'll be out
of the house.

1658
01:17:41,490 --> 01:17:43,292
Pete, drop down and see
if you can see any signs...

1659
01:17:43,292 --> 01:17:45,862
Why don't you drop down
and kiss my pink behind?

1660
01:17:45,862 --> 01:17:47,196
Be careful.

1661
01:17:47,196 --> 01:17:50,700
I want you to be alive
when I break up with you.

1662
01:17:50,700 --> 01:17:52,035
Let me at 'em.

1663
01:17:52,035 --> 01:17:54,938
Damn the torpedoes, please.

1664
01:17:54,938 --> 01:17:58,607
Hey, dropping down.
Oh, oh, that could hurt--
( mumbling )

1665
01:18:02,712 --> 01:18:04,647
It's okay. It's okay, come on.

1666
01:18:04,647 --> 01:18:07,851
He's a regular Sacagawea.

1667
01:18:07,851 --> 01:18:12,355
I jumped down and scouted
the place out like you
said. I did.

1668
01:18:16,025 --> 01:18:18,127
Look, we haven't got a chance
without a gun.

1669
01:18:18,127 --> 01:18:19,628
We've got to get back
into the trophy room.

1670
01:18:19,628 --> 01:18:21,064
We can't.
We just got out of there.

1671
01:18:21,064 --> 01:18:23,332
That's just why we can
take a chance on going
back there.

1672
01:18:23,332 --> 01:18:25,835
Those guards will still
be out looking for you girls.

1673
01:18:25,835 --> 01:18:27,470
Now if we can shake Balleau

1674
01:18:27,470 --> 01:18:29,038
and if we can get back there
before the guards do.

1675
01:18:29,038 --> 01:18:31,240
We can get the guns

1676
01:18:31,240 --> 01:18:32,541
and maybe have a chance
to stay alive long enough

1677
01:18:32,541 --> 01:18:34,710
to find the boat.
Come on.

1678
01:18:34,710 --> 01:18:37,246
Did you see me scouting,
honey? I scouted.

1679
01:18:39,015 --> 01:18:42,485
I haven't seen a co-worker
for weeks. Oh, well.

1680
01:18:42,485 --> 01:18:45,554
I will not let down my vigil.

1681
01:18:47,223 --> 01:18:49,525
There's one guard that's not
out combing the bushes for us.

1682
01:18:49,525 --> 01:18:51,427
Should we jump him, Johnny?

1683
01:18:51,427 --> 01:18:52,796
No, I don't think so.

1684
01:18:52,796 --> 01:18:55,231
I think our best chance
is to try and sneak past him.

1685
01:18:57,901 --> 01:19:00,904
I gots one job,
but I does it well.

1686
01:19:02,405 --> 01:19:05,541
And I eats Robert Reed.

1687
01:19:07,243 --> 01:19:09,545
Hey, mister,
can we go in now?

1688
01:19:09,545 --> 01:19:12,548
All:
He-he-he...

1689
01:19:16,352 --> 01:19:20,689
Maybe I can kill a bush.
Aw, it wouldn't be the same.

1690
01:19:20,689 --> 01:19:23,292
I suppose I should have
kept my townhouse
in Manhattan.

1691
01:19:23,292 --> 01:19:25,128
Well...

1692
01:19:25,128 --> 01:19:28,798
Ah, time for my story.

1693
01:19:28,798 --> 01:19:30,099
Wonder if there's
any of that

1694
01:19:30,099 --> 01:19:34,003
German potato salad
left in the 'fridge.

1695
01:19:34,003 --> 01:19:37,073
( singing in German )

1696
01:19:43,612 --> 01:19:46,049
It's just as I remember it.

1697
01:19:47,383 --> 01:19:50,419
Are you guys ready for this?
Remote control everything.

1698
01:19:53,556 --> 01:19:55,291
