Does he ever take them out
and play with them?

1754
01:23:02,411 --> 01:23:06,282
Just switch 'em on all
at once, you showoff.

1755
01:23:08,317 --> 01:23:09,818
Well, there you have it.

1756
01:23:09,818 --> 01:23:13,956
I call that one
"Lutheran Love ."

1757
01:23:13,956 --> 01:23:15,691
There's plenty of time.

1758
01:23:15,691 --> 01:23:17,793
I've got fudge.

1759
01:23:19,062 --> 01:23:21,164
Strange about these old walls.

1760
01:23:21,164 --> 01:23:22,465
Yeah, what's that?

1761
01:23:22,465 --> 01:23:24,967
The smallest sound 
 is amplified.

1762
01:23:24,967 --> 01:23:29,672
If one sits quite 
 still, one can hear 
 the slightest murmur.

1763
01:23:29,672 --> 01:23:33,008
Sometimes even
the slightest breath.

1764
01:23:33,008 --> 01:23:34,810
( squeals )

1765
01:23:34,810 --> 01:23:37,413
See, I'm suggesting that
there may be someone in here.

1766
01:23:37,413 --> 01:23:42,085
Certain closeness
about this place.
I've never corrected it.

1767
01:23:42,085 --> 01:23:44,087
It helps preserve my trophies.

1768
01:23:44,087 --> 01:23:45,621
Maybe when I retire.

1769
01:23:45,621 --> 01:23:48,191
But at times it does make
breathing difficult.

1770
01:23:48,191 --> 01:23:51,860
He does this twice a day
and once in a while he
actually finds somebody.

1771
01:23:51,860 --> 01:23:55,064
I've sat here so long
that I find I can sit
for hours

1772
